ground=dict(source_ids=['s-proposal-read-admission','s-config-commit','s-tracker','s-conf-progress','s-config-validation','s-read-result'],expectation_ids=['s-read-safe-option','s-node-read-contract','s-raw-read-api','s-simple-demotion-test'],binding_ids=['bind-safe-read-singleton'],derivation='ReadOnlySafe promises linearizable read requests. Node/RawNode ReadIndex promises that the matching read may be processed safely once application advances further than its returned index. For a deterministic register with no intervening later writes, that implies a read invoked after an acknowledged committed write must not return a prior register value when this application condition is met. Demotion is a supported membership operation and StepDownOnRemoval=false is accepted; its role-retention option does not state an exception to safe-read semantics. The check will use actual register application and strict applied>ReadState.Index, not presume index equality sufficient.',applicability='Caller completes storage and application before Advance, applies a committed simple voter demotion, and keeps the demoted learner in service under its public read API. No clock-dependent lease mode or synthetic reply is needed.',unresolved=['The legal schedule and stale endpoint remain to be constructed and executed.'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Automatic stepdown or higher-term input can prevent the suspected result; include a protection control.','If the learner cannot pass the read barrier without catching up to the completed write, the proposed stale-read endpoint is excluded.'])
